---
components: ["KpiCard"]
description: KPI card answers "how is this metric doing" on one tile: its name, its value, how it changed, its trend, and its target.
---

<script>
  import { Column, Grid, Row } from "carbon-components-svelte";
  import { BulletChart, KpiCard, ShareOfTotal, Sparkline } from "carbon-components-svelte/viz";

  const usd = { style: "currency", currency: "USD", notation: "compact" };
  const revenue = [92, 96, 101, 99, 108, 112, 118, 121, 119, 128];
  const churn = [2.9, 2.8, 2.8, 2.6, 2.7, 2.5, 2.4, 2.3, 2.2, 2.1];
  const latency = [180, 176, 190, 210, 240, 232, 228, 251, 262, 270];
</script>

`KpiCard` is part of the data visualization subpackage. Import it from `carbon-components-svelte/viz` and load `carbon-components-svelte/css/viz.css` alongside `all.css`. With a single-theme stylesheet such as `g100.css`, load the matching `viz-g100.css` instead. The subpackage is experimental: its API may change in a minor release.

It is a [Tile](/components/Tile) that lays out pieces the library already has: a formatted value, a [DeltaIndicator](/components/DeltaIndicator), and slots for a [Sparkline](/components/Sparkline) and a [BulletChart](/components/BulletChart).

## Basic

Pass a `label` and a `value`. `format` takes `Intl.NumberFormat` options or a function, and defaults to compact notation.

<KpiCard label="Monthly revenue" value={1280000} format={usd} />

## Delta

Set `delta` for the change against a baseline, and `deltaLabel` to say which. `deltaFormat` is `"percent"` by default. Set `positive` to `"down"` for metrics where lower is better: the arrow still follows the sign, and only the color changes.

<Grid narrow padding>
  <Row>
    <Column sm={4} md={4} lg={8}>
      <KpiCard label="Monthly revenue" value={1280000} format={usd} delta={0.123} deltaLabel="vs last month" />
    </Column>
    <Column sm={4} md={4} lg={8}>
      <KpiCard
        label="Churn"
        value={0.021}
        format={{ style: "percent", maximumFractionDigits: 1 }}
        delta={-0.004}
        deltaLabel="vs last month"
        positive="down"
      />
    </Column>
  </Row>
</Grid>

## Trend and target

Put a graphic in the `chart` slot and another in the `footer` slot. The chart is hidden from assistive technology, since the value and the delta already say what it shows, so give the footer graphic its own `label`. Size the graphic with its own props, such as a sparkline's `width` and `height`.

<Grid narrow padding>
  <Row>
    <Column sm={4} md={4} lg={5}>
      <KpiCard label="Monthly revenue" value={1280000} format={usd} delta={0.123} deltaLabel="vs last month">
        <Sparkline slot="chart" values={revenue} fill width={240} height={48} />
        <BulletChart slot="footer" value={1.28} target={1.5} max={2} size="sm" label="Against a 1.5M target" />
      </KpiCard>
    </Column>
    <Column sm={4} md={4} lg={5}>
      <KpiCard
        label="Churn"
        value={0.021}
        format={{ style: "percent", maximumFractionDigits: 1 }}
        delta={-0.004}
        deltaLabel="vs last month"
        positive="down"
      >
        <Sparkline slot="chart" values={churn} color="success" width={240} height={48} />
        <ShareOfTotal slot="footer" value={21} total={1000} suffix="of accounts" size="sm" label="Churned accounts" />
      </KpiCard>
    </Column>
    <Column sm={4} md={4} lg={6}>
      <KpiCard label="p95 latency" value={270} format={(v) => `${v} ms`} delta={0.19} deltaLabel="vs last week" positive="down">
        <Sparkline slot="chart" values={latency} color="error" width={240} height={48} />
        <BulletChart slot="footer" value={270} target={250} max={400} bands={[200, 300]} size="sm" label="Against a 250 ms objective" />
      </KpiCard>
    </Column>
  </Row>
</Grid>

## Link

Set `href` to make the whole card a link, which suits a dashboard whose cards open a report.

<KpiCard label="Open incidents" value={7} delta={-3} deltaFormat="number" deltaLabel="vs yesterday" positive="down" href="#" />

## Loading

Set `loading` while the value is on its way. A skeleton holds the value's place, so nothing jumps when it lands, and the card is marked busy.

<KpiCard label="Monthly revenue" loading />

## Custom value

Fill the `value` slot to write the value yourself. It receives `formattedValue`.

<KpiCard label="Uptime" value={0.9992} format={{ style: "percent", maximumFractionDigits: 2 }}>
  <svelte:fragment slot="value" let:formattedValue>{formattedValue} <small>this quarter</small></svelte:fragment>
</KpiCard>

## Accessibility

Everything that matters is text: the label, the value, and the delta, which says its direction in words. The `chart` slot is hidden from assistive technology because it repeats them. A missing value is a dash, not a zero. With an `href` the card is a single link named by its contents.
